(BAS-44 - the Caution example, LANGUAGE.md:174-182. `batch` is undeclared
 in the manual's copy; declaring it as [1, 2] is what makes the documented
 output `1 2 1 2 batch done` reachable. The blank line closes the While
 right after the nested For each closes itself, so `print "batch done"`
 runs ONCE, after the loop - not once per batch as the indentation
 suggests.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox BAS-44.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   1
   2
   1
   2
   batch done
)
a list called batch is [1, 2].
a number called round is 0.
While round is less than 2,
    the round is round add 1,
    For each item in batch,
        print item.

    print "batch done".
